You go through the wall of tall odorous plants. Strong sickly sweet smell surrounds you from all sides, you shroud in it. It feels like you don't draw stems apart, but the very wall of smell, almost tangible. It's very damp here and the ground is slippery. But the objective seems so close, and you're stubbornly marching forward. 
Despite inconveniences, you advance forward pretty fast. It's strange, but you have no more worries about your fate, even scary night in the forest comes to mind as if it happened long ago with somebody else. Somehow you start thinking, that as soon as you reach water, you adventure is going to be over, you find Snoopy and go home to take a nap.
Yeah, it's a good idea - to take a nap... Slight wind is blowing, waves are running through the meadow, ground doesn't seem damp any more. Maybe you should really take a nap. Just half an hour... 